TI  - Fuzzy-Enhanced Deep Learning Model for Robust Cardiac Disease Prediction using CFDLNet Algorithm
PY  - 2025
T2  - 2025 4th International Conference on Smart Technologies and Systems for Next Generation Computing, ICSTSN 2025
DO  - 10.1109/ICSTSN67075.2025.11398016
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105035553900?origin=resultslist
AB  - Cardiac disease continues to be a major contributor to global mortality, highlighting the urgency of timely and precise prediction to enhance patient outcomes. Traditional machine learning and deep learning techniques have shown promising outcomes in predicting cardiac diseases, but their accuracy is influenced by noisy clinical data, imbalanced features and lack of interpretability. To address these issues, this paper introduces a novel algorithm named CFDLNet (Cardiac Disease Prediction based on Fuzzy-Enhanced Deep Learning Network) which involves using fuzzy logic with deep learning to achieve robust and stable prediction outcomes. Fuzzy preprocessing handles uncertainties and ambiguity in medical records, while the deep learning architecture predicting nonlinear relationships among clinical parameters. The interpretability of fuzzy logic and the representation power of deep learning enables CFDLNet to reduce misclassification, and show generalization with various datasets. Experiments on benchmark heart disease datasets show that CFDLNet significantly outperforms classical machine learning and recent deep learning models achieving an accuracy of 97.36%, precision of 96.34%, recall of 95.65% and F1- Score of 93.87%. The results indicate that CFDLNet offers an explainable and predictable framework of forecast which may be implemented in clinical decision support systems to detect the cardiac disease in real-time.  © 2025 IEEE.
