AB  - Breast Cancer has become one of the very crucial disease, increasing the mortality rate among woman at an early age worldwide. Therefore, early detection and timely treatment have become increasingly important in the field of medical science. Artificial Intelligence is now widely used for developing models which supports doctors in early detection of breast cancer. In this study, deep learning models are used for classification and prediction of breast cancer. For implementation image data are taken from Mendeley Database. Initially, a Convolutional Neural Network(CNN) is used to classify the images into Cancer and non-cancer with an accuracy of 84.94%. To increase the performance, the EfficientNetB0 model from the EfficientNet family is used. The performance of EfficientNetB0 is much better than the CNN model with the accuracy increased to 93%. However, the key limitation of EfficientNetB0 is that some of the cancer images are misclassified as non-cancer, which will be addressed in future study. © 2025 IEEE.
