TI  - Hybrid dense block convolutional transformers for lung cancer detection and severity analysis
PY  - 2025
T2  - Transforming Healthcare: Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, and 5G Innovations for Enhanced Patient Care
SP  - 224
EP  - 246
DO  - 10.1201/9781003535843-11
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105023737259?origin=resultslist
AB  - The application of artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) in diagnostics and disease management is revolutionizing the medical field by offering accurate disease detection and disease diagnosis more effectively than before. AI and ML techniques were employed to detect diseases from mild stages to severe diseases by exploring difficult patterns in diseased datasets, medical images, and genomes from the CT scans and MRI images. The initial stages of diseases can previously be detected and diagnosed, especially the deadly diseases such as cancer, tumors, cardiovascular diseases, and nerve disorders. They improve the accuracy, precision, and specificity in diseases detection and diagnosis, prevent the false detection and diagnosis, and reduce the death rate out of detection in the severe stages. AL and ML techniques offer flexibility in the diagnosis of diseases by analyzing the stages of diseases and their impacts on patients. They also monitor the response from the patients for the distinct medical therapies. AI techniques inspect persistent diseases like lung, heart, and the diabetics. The patient is under complete surveillance for the effective diagnosis of diseases by adopting themselves for the treatment. The detection of impacts of diseases in the patients is effectively analyzed to provide the responsive treatment and prevent adverse outcomes. The hybridization of AI and ML techniques, Optimal Compact convolutional transformers, which is a hybridization of vision transforms and the convolutional neural networks, outperforms the existing convolutional neural networks models as well as the distinct transformers models. The hybridization of CNN and vision transformers along with the residual convolutional blocks not only improves the precision in disease detection and diagnosis but also reduces the medical expenses by upgrading the resource assignments and saves time from the misclassification in the detection and diagnosis. Dense block convolutional transformer module is proposed for lung cancer detection in which the parameters are immensely reduced along with the minimal time consumption that offers impressive performance than other prevailing models in disease detection and analysis. It expands the lifespan of the patients by earlier detection and diagnosis of diseases. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, K. Srinivasan, Jude Hemanth, and V. Rukkumani; individual chapters, the contributors.
