TI  - A Hybrid Deep Learning Framework for Multi-Class Lung Disease Classification
PY  - 2026
T2  - 2026 IEEE International Conference for Convergence in Computing Technology, I3CTCON 2026
DO  - 10.1109/I3CTCON68242.2026.11507770
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105041645839?origin=resultslist
AB  - Lung diseases remain a leading cause of morbidity and mortality worldwide, and timely, accurate diagnosis is critical for effective treatment. Although chest X-ray (CXR) imaging is widely used, manual interpretation is prone to human error, and existing machine learning and deep learning models often fail to simultaneously capture both local texture variations and global contextual features. Addressing this gap, this study proposes Multi-Stream Lung Disease Classifier (MSLDC), a novel framework designed to integrate gradient-based edge detection, multi-scale convolutional neural networks with channel-spatial attention, and a streamlined Vision Transformer for comprehensive multi-channel feature extraction. The objectives were to enhance sensitivity to subtle abnormalities, improve feature representation, and achieve robust multi-class classification across diverse lung disease categories. MSLDC was evaluated on two publicly available datasets, i.e., Chest X-Ray images dataset and IEEE data port dataset along with a combined dataset, achieving 99.95%, 99.95%, and 99.96% on the combined dataset, achieving better performance, minimal misclassifications, and high clinical reliability. These findings indicate that MSLDC effectively addresses current limitations and offers a scalable, accurate solution for automated lung disease detection. © 2026 IEEE.
