TI  - Advanced Deep Learning Framework for Ultrasound Breast Cancer Classification Using CNNs and Vision Transformers with Explainable AI
PY  - 2026
T2  - 2026 IEEE 2nd International Conference on Quantum Photonics, Artificial Intelligence and Networking, QPAIN 2026
DO  - 10.1109/QPAIN69676.2026.11546369
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105043098988?origin=resultslist
AB  - Breast cancer remains a leading cause of mortality among women worldwide, making early and accurate classification crucial. Despite being an essential diagnostic tool, manual interpretation of ultrasound images is time-consuming and prone to error. Leveraging Explainable AI (XAI) techniques, this study presents an advanced deep learning framework for automated breast cancer classification using convolutional neural networks (CNNs) and Vision Transformers (ViTs). Utilizing a publicly available dataset of 9,016 annotated breast ultrasound images, we evaluate several state-of-the-art architectures, including DenseNet201, ResNeSt50, ConvNeXtV2, ViT-B16, ViTB/32, Swin Transformer V2, and RepVGG. Compared with existing approaches, our proposed ViT-B/32 model surpasses them, achieving 99.67% validation accuracy, 0.9999 AUC, and minimal misclassifications. Transparency for medical practitioners is enhanced through attention mechanisms and LIME-based interpretability, providing clinically meaningful insights into model decision-making. Extensive evaluations, including confusion matrix analysis and t-SNE visualization, validate our framework's robustness. The results demonstrate that transformer-based models integrated with XAI offer superior interpretability and accuracy, making them highly suitable for clinical applications in breast cancer diagnosis. © 2026 IEEE.
