AB  - Only an early diagnosis can solve pneumonia that has been one of the major causes of death in the world. The specified deep-learning-based novel method employed in the given paper is the one of pneumonia detection on the background of the chest X-ray and CT scan image that is based on CNN, ResNet, MobileNet, and DenseNet models. The common goal will be to classify the photographs of the CT scan and chest X-ray as either normal or pneumonia, and that will be further supported by the diagnosis of the same. The system has also an intelligent validation system that enhances the credibility of the system and that has the capacity to detect irrelevant images e.g. the non-medical images. MobileNet model will be applied to this end in order to isolate irrelevant images in medical X-rays and CTs. DenseNet is not an exception in the system since it has shown enormous potential in the medical images classification field due to its feature reuse that allows fewer figures to obtain a higher performance, and, therefore, its beneficial use. It is a process of multi-step verification that guarantees the accuracy of the pneumonia recognition and subsequent elimination of the unnecessary ones and prevents misclassification. The models are trained and evaluated with a great amount of a large number of X-ray and CT scan images of the chest leading to the achievement of a high accuracy and stability in classification. The suggested technique may play a significant role in timely and reliable detection of pneumonia by the physicians, and at the same time, the issue of correct medical images handling can be discussed. © 2026 IEEE.
