AB  - Cancer remains a leading global health challenge, with breast and lung cancer contributing significantly to morbidity and mortality rates. Early and accurate classification of cancer type and severity is crucial for effective treatment planning. This study proposes a Multi-Head Swin Transformer model for classifying cancer type (breast vs. lung) and cancer severity (normal, benign, malignant) using Mini-DDSM (breast cancer) and IQOTH/NCCD (lung cancer) datasets. The model was trained using an 8 0 - 1 0 - 1 0 % data split and assessed based on accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score metrics. Experimental outcomes reveal 100 % accuracy in cancer type classification, 98.17 % in lung cancer severity classification, and 70.10 % in breast cancer severity classification, with misclassifications primarily occurring between benign and malignant breast cancer. The findings highlight our model's robustness in lung cancer classification and the need for improved feature extraction techniques for breast cancer differentiation. Future enhancements include integrating multi-scale attention mechanisms and leveraging larger datasets to refine classification performance further  © 2025 IEEE.
