AB  - Peripartum cardiomyopathy is an uncommon disorder of unknown cause, which is characterized by left ventricular systolic dysfunction during the last month of pregnancy or within 5 months of the postpartum period. It is a disease of exclusion with heterogeneous pathogenetic mechanisms and varying pathological features. An elderly primigravida with gestational hypertension presented with progressive dyspnea due to left ventricular hypokinesia. At autopsy, the heart revealed histomorphological features of dilated cardiomyopathy. © The Editor(s) (if applicable) and The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2022.
