AB  - The proceedings contain 32 papers. The topics discussed include: adaptive weighted multi-view clustering; Bayesian active questionnaire design for cause-of-death assignment using verbal autopsies; modeling multivariate biosignals with graph neural networks and structured state space models; token imbalance adaptation for radiology report generation; missing values and imputation in healthcare data: can interpretable machine learning help?; revisiting machine-learning based drug repurposing: drug indications are not a right prediction target; multi-modal pre-training for medical vision-language understanding and generation: an empirical study with a new benchmark; SRDA: mobile sensing based fluid overload detection for end stage kidney disease patients using sensor relation dual autoencoder; towards the practical utility of federated learning in the medical domain; self-supervised pretraining and transfer learning enabletitlebreak flu and COVID-19 predictions in small mobile sensing datasets; and collecting data when missingness is unknown: a method for improving model performance given under-reporting in patient populations.
