TI  - A New Hybrid Bagging Ensemble Machine Learning Model to Identify Parkinson's Diseases Based on Voice Data
PY  - 2024
T2  - Proceedings - International Conference on Computational Intelligence and Networks
DO  - 10.1109/CINE63708.2024.10881138
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/86000230939?origin=resultslist
AB  - Parkinson's disease is chronic, progressive neurological disorder that affects millions of people worldwide and significantly lowers their quality of life. It is often diagnosed through clinical sign assessment and medical monitoring. This includes characterising a range of motor symptoms. However, because they rely on the assessment of motions that are occasionally imperceptible to human sight and hence challenging to identify, potentially misclassifying patients, traditional diagnostic techniques may be vulnerable to subjectivity. Early Parkinson's disease (PD) related non-motor symptoms may be quite mild and have a variety of underlying causes. As a result, these symptoms are frequently disregarded, which makes an early PD diagnosis difficult. Given that Parkinson's disease is unexpected and incurable, automatic diagnosis of this disease based on voice recordings may be an advancement over more expensive and ruling diagnostic experiments and also an innovative approach. Essential patterns will be found by analyzing the vocal recordings gathered, and prompt recommendations for suitable therapies will be very beneficial. This study suggested a machine learning model that uses a new bagging based ensemble classification model (H Bagging) to maximize model performance in order to distinguish healthy individuals from those who have the illness. The suggested approach produces results that are extremely competitive and has the potential to be improved upon and applied in a practical situation.  © 2024 IEEE.
