AB  - The most vicious malady among women is breast cancer. The expeditious detection will aid to escalate the survival rate and also dwindle the mortality rate due to breast cancer. A machine learning-based system is proposed for the explicit diagnosis of breast cancer. Support vector machine (SVM), K-nearest neighbour (K-NN), Naive Bayes (NB), decision tree (DT) and random forest (RF) are being used for the development of the model. The significant features for the model are selected by using least absolute shrinkage and selection operator (Lasso). Accuracy, misclassification, sensitivity, specificity, F1 score, Mathew’s correlation coefficient (MCC) and Youden’s index (J) were calculated for model diagnosis assessment. © 2022, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd.
