AB  - Lungs of people are susceptible to developing cancer; according to WHO, cancer is a leading cause of death worldwide, accounting for nearly 10 million deaths in 2020, and lung cancer alone has caused 1.8 million deaths. To tackle the lung cancer, this paper proposes a 3D U-Net model, which can be utilized to diagnose cancer on CT scans. In the preprocessing step, it converts lung nodule CT scans in DICOM format to PNG format for the purpose of training the model. After that, this study employs 3-dimensional U-Net model, segmentation algorithm, to detect all possible areas of lung nodules on the CT scan. Since lung nodules might be misclassified, this paper introduces a convolutional neural network to classify real and fake lung nodules. The experimental results demonstrate that ACC reached 93.8%. Furthermore, it has been noted that AUC has 0.9358, which means the model has good classification ability for positive and negative cases. © 2021 IEEE.
