AB  - COVID-19 is a serious challenge that the world is facing today. Though vaccination has reduced the mortality rates, it still negatively impacts people's health and quality of life. Comorbidities and old age increase the risk of mortality. Early detection and isolation of infected people is crucial to prevent the sickness from spreading. This is an important step in the fight against COVID. Though RTPCR is widely used to test COVID, the associated risk of false detection and misclassification is high. The use of chest X-rays is critical diagnosing COVID-19. Automated analysis of chest X-rays can save time and effort in detecting the disease, which can be extremely valuable to the medical community. Deep learning (DL) models are mathematical models that can effectively analyze and classify images by automatically extracting highly discriminative features. This paper system based on deep convolutional neural network (CNN) is proposed to distinguish COVID-19 from normal instances, as well as other lung disorders with overlapping characteristics that include Pneumonia, and Tuberculosis. © 2022 IEEE.
