AB  - Mortality Prediction Models yield probabilities of hospital mortality for patients at admission, 24, and 48 hours in the ICU. Each probability is derived from an easily computed statistical model using readily available clinical information. A 72-hour model is under development. Classification of patients based on their observed and predicted mortality results in misclassification rates similar to other methods. Current research is focused on developing a misclassification model. The small group of patients at high risk of misclassification would be identified and predictions of mortality reserved for the larger group of patients for whom such predictions are more reliable.
