SP  - 654
EP  - 661
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/0020372255?origin=resultslist
AB  - A 39-year-old woman got out from the scene of a fire started in her own house. After she walked unsteadily for about 50 m, she then became unconscious. Although she was immediately hospitalized, she died of unknown cause after 4 days. The body was autopsied in our laboratory to find out the cause of death. However no findings on the cause of death were found macroscopically. At the autopsy some organic solvents which smelt of kerosene were noticed in the stomach contents. The analytical investigation showed the organic solvents not to be kerosene components, but they were identified as ethylbenzene, p-, m- and o-xylenes by GLC and GC-MS. Since large amounts of alkylbenzenes were detected not only in the stomach contents but in the adipose tissue, brain, liver and other tissues and there was no disease or injury, her cause of death was finally judged to be alkylbenzene poisoning.
