AB  - Granulomatous angiitis of the central nervous system occurred in a 43-year-old male presenting with recurrent intracerebral hemorrhage confirmed by computed tomography. A surgical specimen ob tained at hematoma removal revealed granulomatous angiitis. Systemic investigation found no underlying cause for the hemorrhage. Although the incidence is very low, this condition should be con sidered in cases of recurrent intracerebral hemorrhage with unknown cause. When surgery is in dicated, biopsy of the brain and leptomeninges should be obtained, because involvement of the lep tomeninges has occurred in virtually all autopsy cases. © 1992, The Japan Neurosurgical Society. All rights reserved.
