TI  - The causes of death in France, 1925-1978: reclassification according to the Eighth Revision of the International Classification of Diseases
PY  - 1990
T2  - Measurement and analysis of mortality
SP  - 295
EP  - 327
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/0025590263?origin=resultslist
AB  - Each successive revision of the International Classification of Diseases (ICD) has introduced a discontinuity in the cause-of-death statistics which makes it very difficult to assess the changes over a long period of time. Elsewhere, we proposed a method for reclassifying deaths according to two criteria, aetiology and anatomy, to reconstruct statistical series which were consistent with, but completely different from any that might be drawn directly from the ICD, results were limited to the period 1958-74, which is covered in France by the Seventh and Eighth Revisions of the ICD. This work has now been completed, and we have an aetiological-anatomical reclassification of all deaths in France between 1925 and 1978. This chapter describes the difficulties we encountered in the course of this intermediate stage and procedures we adopted for dealing with them. We describe the problems in establishing consistency between successive revisions of the ICD, outline the reconstruction of the complete statistical series based on the Eighth Revision of the ICD, and discuss the treatment of ill-defined or unspecified causes of death. -from Authors
