VL  - 142
IS  - 4
SP  - 257
EP  - 261
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/0019329969?origin=resultslist
AB  - With the object of investigating the bases for the diagnoses in the death certificates, information was collected in the form of clinical information, descriptions of autopsies etc. concerning 373 representative selected deaths. In addition, 3 different assistants undertook coding of the 373 death certificates independently of one another. This review revealed very poor agreement between the 3 codings. On the other hand, the account revealed that the bases for certain diagnoses were very weak. With the criteria employed in this account, the causes of death must be considered to be unknown in one fourth of the cases in which acute myocardial infarction was stated as the cause of death. In addition, heart disease was wrongly coded as the basic cause of death in a series of cases. A major reason for this was an error in the sequence of the diagnoses on the death certificate. With the criteria laid down in this account for determination of the cause of death, an increasing number of deaths will be included in the death certificates under unknown cause of death. It is emphasized, however, that until new directives have been elaborated, doctors must employ the criteria hitherto employed when stating the diagnoses in the death certificates.
